  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food Security and Livelihoods - Asia Regional</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NPA in Asia regional supports crisis-affected individuals by ensuring their immediate food needs are met while strengthening their long-term resilience. The humanitarian response uses a combination of gender-, age-, and disabilities sensitive assistance modalities. In areas where markets remain accessible, households receive multipurpose cash assistance to address urgent food requirements. In locations where market access is limited but supply chains allow, affected populations receive in-kind food distributions and essential non-food items. Alongside emergency support, NPA helps communities begin recovering their livelihoods. Individuals participate in livelihood empowerment activities that include community-based environmentally sustainable agricultural support, climate-adaptation initiatives, and small-scale vocational skills training. These activities aim to improve self-reliance and reduce vulnerability to future shocks.</narrative>
  </description>
